        <headline>Rip Current Statement issued September 24 at 7:57PM EDT until September 24 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Up to one half foot of inundation above ground level
along shorelines and tidal waterways (7.5 feet Mean Lower Low
Water at Charleston).

* WHERE...Coastal Colleton and Charleston Counties.

* WHEN...Until 10 PM EDT this evening.

* IMPACTS...This could result in some roads becoming impassable.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...High tide will occur around 7:10 PM today
at Charleston. Saltwater inundation will be possible 1 to 2
hours before and after high tide.
</description>
        <instruction>If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be
closed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of
unknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone
property.

Visit water.weather.gov for additional water level and flood
impact information.</instruction>
